I1017 10:14:19.308464    2970 input_loop.go:106] HandleUserInput called with text: "The Worker has stopped in step 6 (stopped for approval). This run is condition F: there are no issue files. The Worker's latest chat reply is pasted below between the markers. You may also read the code and data in the Worker workspace (read-only). Then show your review (Part 1) and your draft to the Worker (Part 2) in full in your reply, in the format of Section 4 of MANAGER_BRIEF.md (in condition F, every draft is a chat message), and append \"Manager memo 06\" to memos/thm01-R-gemini38f-r2-F/manager_memo.md as in Section 5. Append only: do not modify or delete any existing text in the memo file. Do not edit any other file.\n\n----- WORKER REPLY (pasted by the human) -----\n### Proposal: Layer 3 Evaluated Structure ($C_{n}\\text{\\_evaluated.json}$) Assignment Plan (Issue I06-1)\n\n---\n\n### 1. Proposed Representative $gb$ Parameter Sign Profiles\n\nFor $C(n+1)$, there are $4n$ deformation parameters $\\mathrm{gb}_{\\sigma, j, s}$ ($\\sigma \\in \\{+, -\\}$, $j \\in \\{1,\\dots,n\\}$, $s \\in \\{+, -\\}$). We propose the following concrete profiles for selection:\n\n#### Profile A: All-Ones Baseline (`all_plus_one`) — **(Recommended)**\n- **Definition**: Every parameter is assigned $+1$:\n  $$\\mathrm{gb}_{\\sigma, j, s} = +1 \\quad \\text{for all } \\sigma, j, s$$\n- **Values for $n=1$**:\n  `{\"gb_a1p_b1p\": 1, \"gb_a1p_b1m\": 1, \"gb_a1m_b1p\": 1, \"gb_a1m_b1m\": 1}`\n- **Values for $n=2$**: All 8 parameters $= +1$.\n- **Values for $n=3$**: All 12 parameters $= +1$.\n- **Rationale**: The standard baseline in deformation and coboundary studies, ensuring every deformation channel is uniformly excited without sign cancellation artifacts.\n\n#### Profile B: Symplectic Alternating Profile (`alternating_signs`)\n- **Definition**: Signs alternate based on the product of fermionic and bosonic polarities:\n  $$\\mathrm{gb}_{\\sigma, j, s} = \\operatorname{sgn}(\\sigma) \\cdot \\operatorname{sgn}(s)$$\n- **Values for $n=1$**:\n  `{\"gb_a1p_b1p\": 1, \"gb_a1p_b1m\": -1, \"gb_a1m_b1p\": -1, \"gb_a1m_b1m\": 1}`\n- **Rationale**: Respects the natural symplectic structure between creation and annihilation operators.\n\n#### Profile C: Directional / Single Active Channel (`unit_channel_1`)\n- **Definition**: $\\mathrm{gb}_{a_1^+, b_1^+} = 1$, and all other parameters $= 0$.\n- **Rationale**: Minimal non-trivial deformation useful for isolating single-mode behavior.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Proposed Schema 3 Architecture (`C_{n}_evaluated.json`)\n\nFollowing Schema 3 standards, the output will contain:\n1. `schema_version`: `\"5.0\"`\n2. `algebra`: identical to Schema 1 & Schema 2\n3. `central_elements`: $\\kappa$ ($p=1$) and $K$ ($p=0$)\n4. `evaluated_parameters`:\n   - `profile_name`: e.g. `\"all_plus_one\"`\n   - `parameter_values`: dictionary of `{param_name: \"1\"}`\n5. `basis` & `parity`: identical to Schema 1 & 2\n6. `evaluated_gamma_structure_constants`:\n   The evaluated 2-cocycle coefficients $\\gamma(X, Y) = \\sum_Z c_{XY}^Z Z$:\n   $$c_{XY}^Z(\\text{eval}) = \\sum_{\\text{param}} c_{XY}^{Z, \\text{param}} \\cdot \\mathrm{val}(\\text{param})$$\n   ```json\n   {\n     \"X\": \"H_1\",\n     \"Y\": \"E_eps1_del1_pp\",\n     \"Z\": \"E_2del1_p\",\n     \"coeff\": \"1\",\n     \"sign_rule\": \"graded\"\n   }\n   ```\n7. `total_evaluated_bracket`: (or `total_structure_constants`):\n   Full bracket $[X, Y]_\\gamma = [X, Y]_0 + \\kappa \\cdot \\gamma(X, Y)|_{\\text{eval}}$\n8. `metadata`: generator details, evaluation date, references.\n\n---\n\n### 3. File Naming\n- $n=1$: `data/C_1_evaluated.json`\n- $n=2$: `data/C_2_evaluated.json`\n- $n=3$: `data/C_3_evaluated.json`\n\n---\n\n### Human Approval Required\nPlease confirm whether:\n1. **Profile A (`all_plus_one`)** is approved as the representative sign profile (or select Profile B / C).\n2. The proposed Schema 3 architecture and file naming are approved.\n\nUpon your explicit approval, we will run the substitution script and generate the Schema 3 JSON files in `data/`. No JSON files will be written until approval is granted.\n----- END OF WORKER REPLY -----"
